==Trivia==
*Bikura's name is derived from the Japanese phrase ''bikkura-koita'', meaning "be surprised".
**It may also be a reference to [https://youtu.be/5-TnaZU-gEw Bikkura Pon], a game playable at [https://kurasushi.com/ Kura Revolving Sushi Bar], as [[Toy Boat Graveyard]]'s Japanese name starts with the onomatopoeia ''ponpon''.
*The ''Ma Kaiiki'' part of the Japanese name, Ma Kaiiki Bikkura Minato, literally means "Devil Sea Area", but is also a pun on ''makai'' ("[[The Aku Realms|Devil World]]"). ''Minato'' means harbor.

